{
  "note": "Recorded by hand from https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ram/latest/userguide/shareable.html. The page has 41 per-service tables holding 83 resource-type rows; the first table on the page is a legend for the Yes/No columns and is not data. The 83 rows name 84 resource codes, because the AWS Network Firewall rule group row names both network-firewall:StatefulRuleGroup and network-firewall:StatelessRuleGroup. 82 codes resolve to a resource type; 2 do not (apigateway:Domainnames, s3-outposts:Outpost). rds:Cluster and s3:AccessGrants are spelled in a way resource-types.json does not carry, but each row names its type in words (\"Aurora DB Clusters\" is AWS::RDS::DBCluster, and the S3 row says \"Create and manage S3 Access Grants Instance centrally\"), so both are counted. No two rows resolved to the same id, so nothing was deduplicated. Features 2-5 are subsets of feature 1: they are four different capabilities measured on the same axis, not four counts of the same thing, and each one satisfies covered + excluded = 82. Amazon EC2 capacity reservations are partial for sharing outside the organization because the page says Yes for Capacity Reservations and No for Capacity Blocks in that one cell.",
